//! Ryan Harness Core - headless IDE kernel entry point.
//!
//! This file exists only to hand control to `cli.dtr` and to carry the process
//! exit code. All behaviour lives in the library modules so that the kernel can
//! be linked into a host (LSP server, extension host, test harness) without
//! going through `main`.
//!
//! Exit-code mechanism, measured against forgen 1.3.0:
//!
//!   * the `exit()` builtin is declared in the prelude but **not implemented**:
//!     both `forgen run` and `forgen build` fail codegen with
//!     `unresolved function call 'datara_rt_exit'`.
//!   * `fn main() -> Int` is the working mechanism. Under AOT the returned
//!     value becomes the process exit status (verified: returning 3 yields
//!     status 3). Under `forgen run` the JIT wrapper discards it and the
//!     process always reports 0.
//!
//! Consequence for CI: exit-code assertions must run the AOT binary
//! (`scripts/build.sh` then `build/ryan.exe`), never `forgen run`.

use cli

fn main() -> Int {
    return cli_main()
}
